    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0580" n="1414" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/224a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-18T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 18, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1031. Cable at once any action Dutch Government may take with reference to
                    requisitioning boats. This Government is prepared to act this evening.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
